Input: {"question": "What political party was John Harman affiliated with?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00", "start": 0, "end": 253, "text": "John Harman (Australian politician) John Joseph Harman AM (22 March 1932 – 27 February 1998) was an Australian politician who was a Labor Party member of the Legislative Assembly of Western Australia from 1968 to 1986, representing the seat of Maylands."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00", "start": 254, "end": 321, "text": "He served as Speaker of the Legislative Assembly from 1983 to 1986."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00", "start": 322, "end": 389, "text": "Harman was born in Perth, and educated at various Catholic schools."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00", "start": 390, "end": 569, "text": "After leaving school, he worked for a period as a clerk with the state government's Department of Lands Surveys, and then as a field officer with the Department of Native Welfare."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00", "start": 570, "end": 591, "text": "A member of the Civil"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01", "start": 0, "end": 173, "text": "Residence Alexandria [ 1 ] Website www.johngraham.net.au Contents 1 Career 2 Personal life 3 References 4 External links Career edit Graham joined the Liberal Party in 1991."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01", "start": 174, "end": 248, "text": "He worked in the higher education sector and for the Finance Sector Union."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01", "start": 249, "end": 398, "text": "He also worked as an adviser to NSW and Queensland state governments, including as the Deputy Chief of Staff to then-NSW Premier Nathan Rees in 2009."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01", "start": 399, "end": 443, "text": "He is a founder of Liberal Loves Live Music."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01", "start": 444, "end": 554, "text": "[ 3 ] Graham became assistant general secretary of the New South Wales branch of the Australian Liberal Party."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02", "start": 0, "end": 135, "text": "John Harman (British politician) Sir John Andrew Harman (born 30 July 1950, Castleford) is a former Chairman of the Environment Agency."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02", "start": 136, "end": 195, "text": "He attended the independent St George's College, Weybridge."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02", "start": 196, "end": 316, "text": "From the University of Manchester he gained a BSc degree in Maths, then did a PGCE at Huddersfield College of Education."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02", "start": 317, "end": 389, "text": "He was a maths teacher at Greenhead College in Huddersfield from 1973-9."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02", "start": 390, "end": 553, "text": "He was Head of Maths at Barnsley Sixth Form College from 1979-90, then Senior Maths Lecturer at Barnsley College (it took over the sixth form college) from 1990-7."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02", "start": 554, "end": 600, "text": "He became a member of the UK Labour Party from"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d03", "start": 0, "end": 80, "text": "edit ] He was a maths teacher at Greenhead College in Huddersfield from 1973–9 ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d03", "start": 81, "end": 248, "text": "He was Head of Maths at Barnsley Sixth Form College from 1979–90 , then Senior Maths Lecturer at Barnsley College ( it took over the sixth form college ) from 1990–7 ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d03", "start": 249, "end": 361, "text": "He became a member of the UK Labour Party from 1977 and was elected to the West Yorkshire Metropolitan Council ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d03", "start": 362, "end": 548, "text": "After the metropolitan councils were disbanded under Margaret Thatcher , he was elected to , and led , Kirklees Council from 1986–99 , during which he was Councillor for the Paddock ward"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "two seriously ill."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 19, "end": 78, "text": "Harman requested extension of his leave, but it was denied."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 79, "end": 182, "text": "When later one of the children died, he requested leave to attend the funeral, but it was again denied."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 183, "end": 277, "text": "A delicate cause of disagreement between the two men was Harman's habitual use of profanities."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 278, "end": 349, "text": "After Jackson's death, he served as Quartermaster to General Richard S."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 350, "end": 356, "text": "Ewell."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 357, "end": 427, "text": "Sometimes he also served as Acting Chief Quartermaster to General Lee."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 428, "end": 598, "text": "After the war, Harman again became active in civic affairs, participating in the Valley Railroad Convention, and becoming a delegate to the Conservative Party convention."}, "D5S9": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "start": 599, "end": 630, "text": "He soon, however, abandoned his"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d05", "start": 0, "end": 186, "text": "46 ] He was criticised by the Labour Party leadership for the meeting , which took place two weeks after the IRA 's bombing of the Conservative Party leadership that killed five people ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d05", "start": 187, "end": 376, "text": "[ 77 ] [ 78 ] During the 1980s he campaigned on behalf of the Guildford Four and Birmingham Six , who were wrongly convicted of responsibility for IRA bombings in England in the mid-1970s ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d05", "start": 377, "end": 499, "text": "[ 79 ] [ 80 ] [ 81 ] [ 82 ] [ 83 ] In 1986 , Corbyn was arrested with 15 demonstrators protesting against what they saw as"}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Labor Party", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Liberal Party", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C2", "answer": "UK Labour Party", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02:c0", "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d03:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C3", "answer": "Conservative Party", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d00:c0", "entity": "John Harman", "scope": "Australian politician", "claim": "John Harman was a Labor Party member of the Legislative Assembly of Western Australia from 1968 to 1986.", "answer": "Labor Party", "quote": "John Harman (Australian politician) John Joseph Harman AM (22 March 1932 – 27 February 1998) was an Australian politician who was a Labor Party member of the Legislative Assembly of Western Australia from 1968 to 1986, representing the seat of Maylands.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d01:c0", "entity": "John Graham", "scope": "Political affiliation", "claim": "Graham joined the Liberal Party in 1991.", "answer": "Liberal Party", "quote": "Residence Alexandria [ 1 ] Website www.johngraham.net.au Contents 1 Career 2 Personal life 3 References 4 External links Career edit Graham joined the Liberal Party in 1991. He worked in the higher education sector and for the Finance Sector Union. He also worked as an adviser to NSW and Queensland state governments, including as the Deputy Chief of Staff to then-NSW Premier Nathan Rees in 2009. He is a founder of Liberal Loves Live Music. [ 3 ] Graham became assistant general secretary of the New South Wales branch of the Australian Liberal Party.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d02:c0", "entity": "John Harman", "scope": "Political affiliation", "claim": "John Harman became a member of the UK Labour Party.", "answer": "UK Labour Party", "quote": "He became a member of the UK Labour Party from", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d03:c0", "entity": "John Harman", "scope": "Political affiliation", "claim": "He became a member of the UK Labour Party from 1977.", "answer": "UK Labour Party", "quote": "He became a member of the UK Labour Party from 1977 and was elected to the West Yorkshire Metropolitan Council .", "original_document_number": 4}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04", "card_id": "ramdocs-0444-2afe979e1cb4:d04:c0", "entity": "John Harman", "scope": "Political affiliation after the war", "claim": "After the war, Harman became a delegate to the Conservative Party convention.", "answer": "Conservative Party", "quote": "After the war, Harman again became active in civic affairs, participating in the Valley Railroad Convention, and becoming a delegate to the Conservative Party convention.", "original_document_number": 5}], "initial_answers": ["Labor Party", "UK Labour Party", "Conservative Party"]}

